<speak><prosody pitch="1.31st" rate="1.00">Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy from the sun into chemical energy in the form of glucose.</prosody><break time="520ms"/><break time="120ms"/><prosody pitch="-1.44st" rate="1.03">This occurs when chlorophyll, a green pigment found in plant cells, absorbs sunlight and uses it to power a series of chemical reactions that produce glucose and oxygen.</prosody><break time="520ms"/><break time="120ms"/></speak>